  "coverage_definition": "A rule is executable when the reference machine interprets its program from semantics/transitions.json, the execution vectors run every instruction of that program, and they take every branch the rule declares. The vectors assert the complete transition trace, terminal, and final state. A rule with an unexecuted instruction or untaken branch is pending and is not a conformance oracle. ir_differential_vectors lists the vectors that are also lowered to IR version 6 (semantics/ir.json), structurally verified, and executed by an independent stack executor that must reproduce the rule machine's observable sequence, terminal, and final state.",
